57-// The sheet may have a cap (the one in force on its today): a person's due-total is at most it, and their excess is how far the
58-// sum of their figures is above it (0.00 otherwise; a due-total of n/a is not capped). Every total
59:// of due-totals (the sheet's, a grade's, backing, the export) adds up the capped figures.
60-// A person is active when they have an OPEN or PENDING claim that counts dated within the 30 days up
61-// to and including the sheet's today; the summary counts the active people per grade, retired excluded.
